direction: down
"derived-credit": "derived-credit\nRelease physical guard only after catcher\nrestoration, marker invalidation, caller cleanup and\nroster handoff; an acknowledgement loss retains\noriginal custody"
"execution-owner": "execution-owner\nRegister durable VM/session and root custody before\nentering throw-capable native activation; guard\nidentity is not continuation identity"
"call-catcher": "call-catcher\nPop only the current call catcher; matching return\nperforms fp and PSR0 restoration, mismatched return\npropagates to restored outer catcher"
"storage-commit": "storage-commit\nExclude all active guards, retained exported\nhandles, invocation authorities and roster debt\nbefore VM retirement; separate from run return"
"outer-catcher": "outer-catcher\nExisting cleanup CFUN restores outer catcher before\nR_ALL_INL and conversion cleanup; AT_END lies inside\nTRY success arm and is not all-path finally"
"marker-guard": "marker-guard\nStable guard owns allocated marker and invalidates\nit once on bypass; allocation failure must not\ninvent an initialized marker"
"reload-cleanup": "reload-cleanup\nSpill/reload, conversion resources, result/error\npropagation and any last caller PSTATE access\nprecede stable release; physical guard cannot be\nreplayed by continuation"
"run-participant": "run-participant\nSecondary processor forwards error then participates\nforever in sync ops; only acknowledged\nroster/storage handoff can replace that duty"
"execution-owner" -> "derived-credit"
"execution-owner" -> "call-catcher"
"call-catcher" -> "marker-guard"
"call-catcher" -> "outer-catcher"
"outer-catcher" -> "reload-cleanup"
"reload-cleanup" -> "run-participant"
"marker-guard" -> "derived-credit"
"reload-cleanup" -> "derived-credit"
"run-participant" -> "derived-credit"
"derived-credit" -> "storage-commit"
proof: "SysML -> ASCENT -> QNT / Lean; source + platform OPEN"
"storage-commit" -> proof
gain0: "guard-coverage\nSafety gain; no current throughput claim. CFUN\nconversion cleanup already exists and cannot be counted\nagain"
proof -> gain0
gain1: "session-sharing\nNet work positive only saved lease work exceeds\nreceipt, roots and retention costs; current code is not\nthis comparator"
proof -> gain1
gain2: "caller-retirement\nCan retire duplicate ownership policy, never erase\nrequired semantic cleanup or old-roster duties by\nassertion"
proof -> gain2
gain3: "modern-c-baseline\nZig offers no proved extra GC/session safety or runtime\nsavings here; modern C remains required"
proof -> gain3
